title: RamCharan_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic RamCharan>>
<<SetBGSprite Library>>

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Seeking a quiet place to read and study, Raju visits the school library.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Away from the noise and distractions of his crowded home.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
He hopes to find both educational resources and peaceful atmosphere.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
The hushed atmosphere of the school library envelops him.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
The smell of aging paper and quiet learning creates a sanctuary.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
This contrasts sharply with the chaos of his overcrowded home.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Tall shelves lined with books stretch toward the ceiling like guardians of wisdom.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Soft afternoon light filters through dusty windows.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
The space carries an almost sacred quality.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Angry">>
RamCharan: Quiet!

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Angry">>
RamCharan: This is a library, not your cricket ground.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Irritated">>
RamCharan: If you've come here to meet friends or plan games, you can leave immediately.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: This space is reserved for students who respect learning.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Anxious">>
Raju: Sir, I just came to look at some books.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: I want to read more.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: Maybe find materials that could help with my studies.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: I wasn't planning to disturb anyone or talk about cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Skeptical">>
RamCharan: Books? Hah!

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Disgusted">>
RamCharan: All I ever hear about you from other teachers is cricket, cricket, cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Irritated">>
RamCharan: Your name comes up in staff meetings.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Angry">>
RamCharan: As the boy who dreams of playing instead of focusing on academics.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Skeptical">>
RamCharan: Do you even know what algebra is?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Embarrassed">>
Raju: I... I do like both things, sir.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Anxious">>
Raju: I enjoy cricket, but I know studies are important too.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Cricket is just something I feel I'm naturally good at.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: Something that gives me hope for the future.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Skeptical">>
RamCharan: Good at hitting a ball with a wooden stick, perhaps.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Irritated">>
RamCharan: But will that skill help you pass your exams?

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: Will cricket knowledge get you into college?

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Skeptical">>
RamCharan: Or help you support a family?

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: This library contains the wisdom of centuries.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Confident">>
RamCharan: Mathematics that builds bridges.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Proud">>
RamCharan: Literature that shapes minds.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: History that teaches wisdom.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Confident">>
RamCharan: Science that advances civilization.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: Don't waste your time here unless you're prepared to abandon childish fantasies.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Disappointed">>
Raju: I understand, sir.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: I'm sorry for disturbing you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Irritated">>
RamCharan: Understanding and action are different things, boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: Prove your seriousness through behavior, not words.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Skeptical">>
RamCharan: This library doesn't need another sports-obsessed student.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: Who treats education as secondary to entertainment.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
As Raju exits the library, Ram Charan's harsh words ring in his ears.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
He feels the familiar sting of having his dreams dismissed as childish fantasies.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
The librarian's passionate defense of learning resonates with something deep within him.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Even as the rejection wounds his pride.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
He confronts an uncomfortable question.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Does pursuing cricket represent an escape from responsibilities or a legitimate path toward a meaningful future?

<<set $RamCharan_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===
title: RamCharan_Day2
tags: 
position: -75,-229
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic RamCharan>>
<<SetBGSprite Library>>

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Despite yesterday's harsh rejection, Raju returns to the library.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Determined to prove that his interest in learning is genuine and persistent.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
The library's familiar quiet embraces him as he returns for the second day.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
His determination to prove his intellectual seriousness is strengthened rather than weakened.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
The rows of books seem less intimidating today.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
More like allies in his quest to demonstrate that academic curiosity and athletic passion can coexist.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
He knows that earning the librarian's respect will require more than simple persistence.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
It will demand genuine engagement with learning for its own sake.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Quizzical">>
RamCharan: Back again?

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Skeptical">>
RamCharan: Most boys run away and never return when they receive the kind of honest assessment I gave you yesterday.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Quizzical">>
RamCharan: They prefer easy encouragement to truthful criticism about their misplaced priorities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Sir, I came to read and learn, just like I said yesterday.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Determined>>
Raju: I understand that you think cricket is a distraction.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: But I want to show you that I can be serious about studies too.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I'm not just here to waste time or prove a point.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Neutral">>
RamCharan: Hmm. At least you demonstrate some persistence.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: Which is more than most students show when facing academic challenges.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: But understand something clearly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: Books require respect, careful handling, and genuine engagement with their contents.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Determined>>
Raju: I do respect books, sir.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Neutral">>
Raju: My brother Ramu always tells me that learning is the most important thing we can do.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Determined>>
Raju: That education opens doors that cricket alone never could.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: But cricket... it makes me dream about possibilities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: Dreams... dangerous things.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Worried">>
RamCharan: When they're not properly balanced with practical knowledge and realistic planning.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Disappointed">>
RamCharan: I've seen too many promising students abandon their studies.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Sad">>
RamCharan: Chasing fantasies that lead nowhere.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Quizzical">>
RamCharan: But I've also observed something in your behavior that intrigues me.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Neutral">>
RamCharan: Most boys who receive correction either argue defensively or disappear permanently.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Quizzical">>
RamCharan: You've returned with respectful persistence.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Smiling">>
RamCharan: That suggests character worth investigating.

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Serious">>
RamCharan: How do you plan to prove this commitment to learning?

<<SetCharacterExpression "RamCharan" "Quizzical">>
RamCharan: What approach will you take to demonstrate genuine academic seriousness?

<<AutoAdvance true>>
Make a Choice
<<AutoAdvance false>>

